{"id": "EUVD-2026-101276", "enisaUuid": "f39bfe81-4870-3cfb-a358-bf1ef0296d0b", "description": "@offactory/compress-fonts before 1.1.1 contains an OS command injection vulnerability that allows attackers to execute shell commands by supplying font files with crafted names. Font paths are interpolated unquoted into a FontForge command run through child_process.execSync, so shell metacharacters in file names execute commands with the Node.js process privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:17:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:15:41", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/adamarcanov/compress-fonts/pull/1", "https://github.com/adamarcanov/compress-fonts/commit/12002e5866af2163cd34424baae5a53338951a5d", "https://github.com/adamarcanov/compress-fonts/blob/7b07d20b3125a7bba8f933eeca21f5a09c8fb62a/index.js#L48", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/offactory-compress-fonts-before-1.1.1-os-command-injection-via-font-file-names"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110648", "GHSA-3jqx-74fv-xh4j"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "50aa294d-1904-31d7-95aa-b261fefb4c33", "product": {"name": "compress-fonts", "vendor": {"name": "adamarcanov"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.1.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cb09ed69-5101-397a-bb0a-46815ccad3ba", "vendor": {"name": "adamarcanov"}}], "isExploited": false}